# Keep git's line-ending conversion away from binary files.
#
# Git guesses text-or-binary from the first few kilobytes. A PDF opens with
# "%PDF-" and a long stretch of readable object headers before any compressed
# stream, so the guess comes out wrong: on checkout git rewrote every LF inside
# it as CRLF, and a 8,888-byte file came back from a fresh clone at 9,012 with
# a broken cross-reference table. It still opened, because readers are
# forgiving, which is exactly why nobody would have noticed.
#
# Everything here is matched by extension rather than left to the heuristic.

*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.webp  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.wasm  binary
*.mp4   binary
*.webm  binary
*.mp3   binary
*.wav   binary
*.zip   binary
*.tgz   binary
